    <string name="service_description">Lets SnapKey Map notice when you press the Snap Key and run the action you picked: open an app, take a screenshot, go home, and so on. Android passes it every hardware key press. It acts only on the key you taught it and lets other keys through unchanged. Android also tells it when another app or screen opens, and it uses only the package name of that app, to pause in apps you choose. It does not read what is on your screen.</string>
